{"chunk_id": "d364ce13fcfb", "text": "This section recounts the climactic duel between Bhishma and the Pandava general Sweta during the early phase of the Kurukshetra war. Bhishma devastates Sweta\u2019s chariot, killing his horses and charioteer, forcing Sweta to fight on foot in a rage. Sweta hurls a terrible golden dart and later smashes Bhishma\u2019s chariot with a mace, showing immense valor. A celestial voice then urges Bhishma to seize the destined moment. Even as Pandava heroes like Bhima, Satyaki, Abhimanyu, and Dhrishtadyumna attempt to intervene, Bhishma holds them back and focuses on Sweta. Finally, he releases a divinely empowered arrow that pierces Sweta and kills him. The Pandava army mourns their fallen commander while the Kauravas celebrate, and the armies withdraw for the night, shaken by the ferocity of the combat.\nBhishma defeats and kills the Pandava commander Sweta after a fierce duel despite attempts by other Pandava heroes to intervene.\nThemes: heroic duel, fate and prophecy, battle fury, divine weapons, war morale", "vector": [0.000852704921271652, -0.008864803239703178, -0.003843411337584257, 5.797353514935821e-05, -0.019047347828745842, 0.03186537325382233, -0.013749762438237667, -0.008272485807538033, -0.014029283076524734, -0.02851112373173237, 0.0019100590143352747, 0.020152119919657707, -0.00787317007780075, 0.01489446684718132, 0.008725042454898357, 0.011979463510215282, 0.03157254308462143, 0.014628256671130657, 0.020298536866903305, -0.01874120533466339, -0.005157824605703354, 0.005071306601166725, 0.008784940466284752, 0.04387145861983299, -0.03332953155040741, 0.01879444718360901, 0.020511504262685776, -0.019726183265447617, 0.006482221186161041, -0.020604677498340607, -0.012119224295020103, -0.01888762228190899, -0.011906255967915058, -0.0014250570675358176, -0.0237592700868845, 0.0009708357392810285, -0.002828484633937478, -0.013037649914622307, 0.006332477554678917, 0.0075137862004339695, 0.0010249096667394042, 0.00199990486